From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] gtk4: reveal Journal main view areas from shell action

When Journal is opened through the shell service, its GTK4 child can retain
the visibility state used while minimized during startup. Reassert visibility
for the main view and its owned areas after selecting the stack child.

--- a/src/jarabe/view/service.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/view/service.py
@@ -111,4 +111,10 @@
         journal.set_hexpand(True)
         journal.set_vexpand(True)
         journal.set_visible(True)
+        if journal._main_view is not None:
+            journal._main_view.set_visible(True)
+        if journal._main_toolbox is not None:
+            journal._main_toolbox.set_visible(True)
+        journal._toolbar_area.set_visible(True)
+        journal._canvas_area.set_visible(True)
         return True
